From 5a880fc0eb41652a97aee347947fc9bf6868571a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 07:45:49 -0500
Subject: btrfs: fix off-by-one end offset check in report_setget_bounds()

From: Filipe Manana <fdmanana@suse.com>

[ Upstream commit 08f750d9f8930e4ca053913b5ca3fd49fd9268c9 ]

The addressable range with an extent buffer goes from byte 0 to byte
eb->len - 1, so if a byte address matches eb->len, it's already beyond
the addressable range and we should log that it's bad start address
and not end address.

Fixes: 234fdd2815ce ("btrfs: remove redundant check in up check_setget_bounds")
Reviewed-by: Qu Wenruo <wqu@suse.com>
Reviewed-by: Daniel Vacek <neelx@suse.com>
Signed-off-by: Filipe Manana <fdmanana@suse.com>
Reviewed-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>
Signed-off-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>

[ sashal: Applied the fix in struct-funcs.c because accessors.c doesn't exist here, and the surrounding context differs slightly. ]

Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
---
 fs/btrfs/struct-funcs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/btrfs/struct-funcs.c b/fs/btrfs/struct-funcs.c
index 12455b2b41de8..7d968f857cdb0 100644
--- a/fs/btrfs/struct-funcs.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/struct-funcs.c
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ static bool check_setget_bounds(const struct extent_buffer *eb,
 	if (unlikely(member_offset + size > eb->len)) {
 		btrfs_warn(eb->fs_info,
 		"bad eb member %s: ptr 0x%lx start %llu member offset %lu size %d",
-			(member_offset > eb->len ? "start" : "end"),
+			(member_offset >= eb->len ? "start" : "end"),
 			(unsigned long)ptr, eb->start, member_offset, size);
 		return false;
 	}
-- 
